::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q01::
Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6
Question:
A table has outputs 4, 7, 10, 13 as x increases by 1. Which model type fits best?
{
~A. Quadratic#Quadratic tables have constant second differences, not constant first differences.
=B. Linear#The first differences are constant at 3.
~C. Exponential#Exponential tables have constant ratios, not constant differences.
~D. No model#The constant difference gives clear evidence for a linear model.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q02::
Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6
Question:
A table has outputs 2, 6, 18, 54 as x increases by 1. Which evidence identifies the model?
{
~A. The first differences are constant.#The first differences are 4, 12, and 36, so they are not constant.
~B. The second differences are constant.#The second differences are not constant.
~C. The outputs are all even.#Even outputs do not identify the function family.
=D. The ratios are constant.#Each output is multiplied by 3, so the model is exponential.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q03::
Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.7
Question:
Which context is best modeled by a quadratic function?
{
=A. The area of a square changes as side length changes.#Square area is represented by A\=s².
~B. A runner travels at a constant speed.#Constant speed gives a linear relationship.
~C. A bank account grows by 4% each year.#Repeated percent growth is exponential.
~D. A subscription costs the same amount each month.#A fixed monthly increase is linear.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q04::
Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.6
Question:
Which equation is exponential?
{
~A. y\=5x+2#This is linear because x has power 1.
~B. y\=x²+5#This is quadratic because the variable is squared.
=C. y\=5(2)ˣ#The variable is in the exponent.
~D. y\=5(x-2)²#This is quadratic in vertex form.
}

::ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q05::
Question ID: ALG1_U05_L07_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A1.FN.7
Question:
A phone plan charges 25 dollars plus 10 dollars per gigabyte. Which model type is most appropriate?
{
~A. Quadratic#There is no squared variable or area-like relationship.
=B. Linear#The cost increases by a constant amount per gigabyte.
~C. Exponential#There is no repeated multiplication or percent change.
~D. Random#The constant charge pattern gives a clear linear model.
}

